      "user": "OpenKnowledge",
      "text": "Selected Answer: B. In machine learning for audio, the sample rate is the number of audio samples taken per second, measured in Hertz (Hz) or kilohertz (kHz). It is crucial because it determines the amount of detail captured in the audio and affects data size. ML models require a consistent sample rate across all audio inputs to process the data correctly. A common sampling rate used in training speech models is 16,000 Hz or 16 kHz."
